    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Swer">Swer</ref> 3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-h"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Swer_3.lnote.oe.4"/><pb n="396" ed="#liebermann"/>On ðone Drihten, næs ic æt ræde ne æt dæde, ne gewita ne gewyrhta, ðær man mid unrihte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="††" target="#Swer_3.lnote.oe.dagger2"/> Ñ orf ætferede.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="396" ed="#liebermann"/>Ðæs oðres að, þe mon his orf ætbryideð. On ðone Drihten, næs ic æt ræde ne æt dæde, ne gewita ne gewyrhta, ðær man mid unrihte Ñ orf ætferede.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="397" ed="#liebermann"/>In illo Deo, non fui in consilio uel in actu<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Swer_3.lnote.oe.11"/>, consulens uel agens, ubi per iniustitiam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Swer_3.lnote.oe.12"/> uel facinus abduceretur pecus hoc N.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="397" ed="#liebermann"/>(Eid<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Swer_3.lnote.de.1"/> des anderen [des Beklagten], dem man sein Vieh wegnimmt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Swer_3.lnote.de.2"/>. <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) Bei dem Herrn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Swer_3.lnote.de.3"/> . . ., nicht war ich bei Rath<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Swer_3.lnote.de.4"/> oder<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="††" target="#Swer_3.lnote.de1.dagger2"/> That, weder Mitwisser<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Swer_3.lnote.de.5"/> noch<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†" target="#Swer_3.lnote.de1.dagger"/> Mitwirker da, wo rechtswidrig (oder<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Swer_3.lnote.de.6"/> mit Trug <hi rend="italic">Quadr</hi>.) dem N. Vieh entwendet worden ist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(The oath of the other [the defendant], from whom one takes his cattle. B) By the Lord …, I was not at the counsel or the deed, neither accessory nor accomplice, where cattle was wrongfully (or by fraud, Quadr.) taken from N.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#unattributed" corresp="#wit-h">[I swear] by the Lord, [that] I [the defendant] was not a planner nor a participant, [nor] a witness nor an accomplice, where someone illegally carried off the N. cattle.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="383"><ref target="clause:Ine_17">Ine 17</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="392"><ref target="clause:Ine_25-1">Ine 25.1</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">U: translator unrecorded: check; Here the Quadripartitus read ‘oððe facne’ (compare VI As 1.1 f.). ‘Rath oder That’ and ‘weder … noch’ are alliterating and rhyming pairs.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Swer_3.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">397</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">acta <hi rend="italic">MHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">acta MHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Swer_3.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">397</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">iniustiam <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">iniustiam R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Swer_3.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">396</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Platz für Überschrift frei</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Space left free for a heading</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Swer_3.lnote.oe.dagger2" n="††" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">396</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">oððe facne <hi rend="italic">las hier Quadr.; vgl.</hi> facnes : facinoris <hi rend="italic">VI As.</hi> 1, 1 <hi rend="italic">f.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">oððe facne was read here by Quadr.; cf. facnes : facinoris VI As. 1, 1 f.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Swer_3.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">235</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Das Kapitel umfasst vier alternative Antworten, wie Becwæð drei</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The chapter comprises four alternative answers, as Becwæð comprises three</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Swer_3.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">235</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Vielleicht besser ‘bei dem m. s. V. im Anefang anschlägt’; Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl</hi>. nimmt <hi rend="italic">æt</hi> als dem regierten <hi rend="italic">þe</hi> nachstehende Präposition; ‘with whom discovers’ Thorpe ungenau. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Anefang 16h</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Perhaps better ‘with whom one lays claim to his cattle in Anefang’; Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl</hi>. takes <hi rend="italic">æt</hi> as a preposition following the <hi rend="italic">þe</hi> it governs; Thorpe’s ‘with whom discovers’ is inaccurate. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Anefang 16h</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Swer_3.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">235</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zu ergänzen aus 1. 2 Anfang</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">To be supplied from the beginning of 1. 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Swer_3.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">235</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Der Endreim (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Wb</hi>) ist in Gesetzessprache seltener; Grimm <hi rend="italic">DRA</hi> 13. Dies Paar sonst <hi rend="italic">s. Wb: ræd</hi> 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">End rhyme (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Wb</hi>) is rarer in legal language; Grimm <hi rend="italic">DRA</hi> 13. For this pair elsewhere <hi rend="italic">see Wb: ræd</hi> 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Swer_3.lnote.de1.dagger2" n="††" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">397</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Endreimpaar</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Rhyming pair</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Swer_3.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">235</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dies Paar <hi rend="italic">s</hi>. Duns 6, 2. VIII Atr 27; dem Sinne nach Ine 25, 1; <hi rend="italic">gewitan ne gewyrcean stala</hi> Homil. [Ælfric?] ed. Brotanek <hi rend="italic">Texte Altengl. Lit</hi>. 21</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">For this pair <hi rend="italic">see</hi> Duns 6, 2. VIII Atr 27; in sense Ine 25, 1; <hi rend="italic">gewitan ne gewyrcean stala</hi> Homil. [Ælfric?] ed. Brotanek <hi rend="italic">Texte Altengl. Lit</hi>. 21</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Swer_3.lnote.de1.dagger" n="†" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">397</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Alliterationspaar</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Alliterative pair</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Swer_3.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">235</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Wohl wie in 2 archetyp und von hb ausgelassen; <hi rend="italic">vgl. for nanum facne ac mid folcrihte</hi> I Ew 1, 5</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Probably, as in 2, in the archetype and omitted by hb; <hi rend="italic">cf. for nanum facne ac mid folcrihte</hi> I Ew 1, 5</seg></note>
      </div>
